course: dictionary
lesson: 10009
title: Temper: keeping calm or losing it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Your temper is how quickly you get angry. «A quick temper» means someone gets cross very fast. Context clues help you spot which meaning is used, so read the words around it.
explain: «Laughed at, Toad loses his temper completely.» The words laughed at tell you why Toad got cross, and completely shows how far he went. So «lose your temper» means to get angry and stop being calm.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it in. «Toad keeps his temper» becomes «Toad stays calm», and it still makes sense, so «keep your temper» means to stay calm.
explain: Temper can also be a verb. A blacksmith tempers steel, and a chocolate maker tempers chocolate. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning to choose.
fact: Temper means how easily you get angry, or a sudden fit of anger.
fact: «Lose your temper» means to get angry and stop being calm; «keep your temper» means to stay calm.
fact: «Hot-tempered» means quick to get angry.
fact: A «temper tantrum» is a sudden fit of anger, often shown by shouting or stamping.
fact: To temper something means to make it milder or less strong, or to heat and cool metal or chocolate to make it hard or shiny.
exercise: «Toad keeps his temper, though he finds their jokes poor and clumsy.» What does keeps his temper mean? | Tells a joke | *Stays calm | Gets very angry | Loses his hat
exercise: «Laughed at, Toad loses his temper completely.» What does lose his temper mean? | *Gets angry and stops being calm | Laughs very loudly | Makes a new friend | Goes to sleep
exercise: A blacksmith tempers steel. What does temper mean here? | To paint something bright | To shout at something | *To heat and cool metal to make it hard and strong | To make something milder
test: «A tired brain is worse at controlling temper, so players short of sleep argue more.» What does controlling temper mean? | *Keeping anger under control | Sleeping more | Making a loud noise | Losing a game on purpose
test: «Young children in a temper sometimes do things they regret.» What does in a temper mean? | Ready for a race | Happy and singing | Very tired and sleepy | *In a sudden fit of anger
exam: Raj leaves the game when he is losing, and the sentence says he «rage-quits» because he is in a temper. What does a quick temper mean? | Running very fast | Being quick to get angry | Winning every game easily | *Being very slow to get cross
